  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(440.95pt, 92.9pt, "5")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(443.95pt, 95.42pt, ", and, in certain cases, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 109.46pt, "the temperature")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(145.34pt, 106.94pt, "6")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(148.34pt, 109.46pt, ", as well as charge trapping phenomena in dielectric materials")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(424.03pt, 106.94pt, "7")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(427.03pt, 109.46pt, ". ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 132.62pt, "The use of TEEY data extracted from the literature without detailed knowledge of the corresponding ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 146.66pt, "surface properties is therefore hazardous. It is essential to determine whether the surface was cleaned in ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 160.82pt, "situ or exposed to ambient air and therefore likely contaminated and possibly oxidized. It is also necessary ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 174.86pt, "to assess whether the surface was irradiated long enough during the TEEY measurement for the electron ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 189.02pt, "beam to alter its physicochemical properties. For dielectric materials, the injected and trapped charges, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 203.06pt, "whether positive or negative, may also significantly influence the measured yield. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 226.22pt, "A comprehensive database, based on tabulated values of BSEY and SEY reported in the literature, was ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 240.26pt, "compiled by David D. Joy")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(181.22pt, 237.74pt, "8")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(184.22pt, 240.26pt, ". Although this database has been and continues to be extremely valuable to the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 254.42pt, "scientific community, very limited information is available regarding the condition of the material surfaces, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 268.49pt, "whether contaminated or not, produced under vacuum or not, eroded in situ, and so forth. Furthermore, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 282.65pt, "the database clearly demonstrates, through the large discrepancies sometimes reaching 300 percent in ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 296.69pt, "the TEEY of a single material, the critical influence of surface properties. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 319.85pt, "These considerations illustrate the difficulty of relying on TEEY values reported in the literature. In many ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 333.89pt, "cases, answering the relevant questions is extremely difficult, if not impossible, due to the lack of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 348.05pt, "information regarding the surface state and the measurement conditions typically accompanying ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 362.09pt, "published results. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 385.25pt, "The objective of this work is to provide a coherent set of TEEY data for several materials, or more precisely ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 399.29pt, "for specific surfaces, while supplying the maximum possible information concerning their surface ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 413.45pt, "characteristics.  ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 14.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 446.47pt, "BASIS ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 470.47pt, "Incident electrons interacting with a target undergo elastic scattering, which primarily redistributes their ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 484.63pt, "trajectories, and inelastic scattering, which induces processes such as collective excitations (plasmons) or ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 498.67pt, "individual electronic excitations. In dielectric materials, additional processes arise, including interactions ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 512.83pt, "with phonons and with trapped charges and their associated electric fields, which may even dominate ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 526.87pt, "under certain conditions. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 550.03pt, "Although electron excitations occur along the entire penetration depth of the incident electrons, which ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 564.07pt, "may extend up to approximately one micrometer for primary energies of several tens of keV, only those ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 578.23pt, "excitations produced within a few nanometers of the surface contribute to electron emission into the ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 611.86pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(73.824pt, 614.38pt, " P. Costa Pinto et al, Carbon coatings with low secondary electron yield, Vacuum, Volume 98, 2013, Pages 29-36 ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 623.38pt, "4")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(73.824pt, 625.9pt, " L. Diazet al. Importance of surface morphology on secondary electron emission: a case study of Cu covered with carbon, carbon ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 637.54pt, "pairs, or graphitic-like layers. Sci Rep 13, 8260 (2023).  ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 646.54pt, "5")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(73.824pt, 649.06pt, " N. Bundaleski et al Calculation of the angular dependence of the total electron yield, Vacuum, Volume 122, Part B, 2015, Pages ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 660.58pt, "255-259, ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
